## Summary

Implements Slice #71 as the first governed mutable autoscale boundary on top of #68/#69/#70.

- adds `runnerctl autoscale run-once [owner/repo|.] [--json]`;
- mutation remains opt-in via `RUNNER_AUTOSCALE_ENABLED=true` and disabled by default;
- makes `run-once` a real producer of RunnerOps-owned continuous queue observations;
- persists an actionable deterministic decision before entering the mutating critical section;
- serializes mutation with a per-host non-blocking lock;
- reloads policy, collects a fresh `CapacitySnapshot`, updates queue evidence and re-runs the same deterministic planner under the lock;
- creates `planned` / `started` only when policy, `START_LOCAL`, exact target and registration identity are still current;
- invokes only `runners.sh start <exact-runner>`; never `all`, `group:*`, `ensure`, `add`, `PROVISION_LOCAL` or `BURST_CLOUD`;
- verifies success from fresh structured `CapacitySnapshot` evidence, requiring the same registration identity, systemd-active local state and GitHub `online`; `busy_capacity` is a valid successful postcondition;
- treats lifecycle exit code as evidence rather than proof: a non-zero start can be successful only when the exact structured postcondition is conclusively verified;
- persists correlated decision/action/outcome records and reconciles retained pending `START_LOCAL` actions after restart;
- uses repository-scoped audit reads so controller planning is not coupled to the bounded global history view.

## Scope decision

This PR deliberately ships **one-shot `run-once` only**. Continuous polling, a systemd autoscaler service and public `autoscale enable/disable` remain deferred until the exact mutating path is proven end to end.

No #72 cloud work, #73 local provisioning, generic scheduler framework, Terraform/Kubernetes or LLM scaling logic is introduced.

## Safety invariants

- deterministic planner remains the scaling decision authority;
- no mutation from `INCONCLUSIVE` evidence;
- decision is durable before mutation, while a new `planned` action is created only after lock + fresh revalidation;
- exact local pre-provisioned runner only;
- target registration identity is correlated through the action `external_id`;
- host lock contention performs no lifecycle mutation and creates no new planned action;
- start exit `0` is never sufficient proof of success;
- started-action recovery is reconciliation work and never blindly reissues a second lifecycle start;
- no tokens, environment dumps or arbitrary subprocess output enter the audit store.

## Validation

Hosted contracts cover queue continuity, decision-before-action ordering, lock contention, policy/queue/registration TOCTOU changes, exact-target guards, restart recovery, structured busy/online verification, non-zero lifecycle exit with verified success, audit correlation and regression of #68/#69/#70 plus existing lifecycle/routing contracts.

Normal PR CI does not enable autoscale mutation on the maintainer host. The final real-host acceptance must use a **separate pre-provisioned idle runner**; the self-hosted runner executing CI must not be stopped/recycled to manufacture the scenario.

Closes #71 after hosted validation and controlled real-host dogfood are both satisfied.

