The historical `baseClassUnlocked`, `isClassUnlocked`, `unlockClass`, and `checkDynamicClassUnlocks` replacement ladders are retired from `runtime/js/dicebound.js`. The compatibility runtime retains only thin context/persistence/reveal adapters where side effects still belong outside the pure rules owner.

## Behavior preserved
The extraction freezes the shipped Beta 0.6.6.21 semantics, including:
- one-way persisted unlocks and event-driven commits;
- guardian, Prestige, lifetime/run-stat and Pet gates;
- Rogue/Vampire/Pokémon Trainer/Invoker/Dragoon compound rules;
- Slime class-count/exclusion semantics and dynamic scan ordering;
- Alchemist career potion tracking and the shipped 15-potion threshold;
- CEO/Ouroboros/Frog/Turtle/Ninja live-run thresholds;
- historical duplicate dynamic-attempt ordering and reveal/persistence behavior;
- no new RNG draws, no balance redesign and no save/checkpoint redesign.

Registry metadata is reconciled to current runtime truth: Alchemist now advertises 15 potion uses and Rouge 10 Prestige points.

## Proof already completed on the exact PR tree
- `tools/test_class_unlock_rules.js` — deterministic class-unlock contract;
- existing `tools/test_0631_progression_slime_gear.js` regression;
- new `tools/test_class_unlock_extraction_boundary.py` shadow-owner/boundary guard;
- runtime architecture validator: 68 modules (67 extracted + 1 compatibility monolith), zero duplicate top-level functions;
- asset architecture validator;
- version identity validation for Beta 0.6.6.22;
- JS syntax + `git diff --check`.

Monolith after extraction: **769,124 bytes / 7,514 physical lines** (validator count 7,515), down from roughly 777,065 bytes / 7,620 lines on the reconciled 0.6.6.21 baseline.

The normal PR workflow must still prove the full Windows source/Edge/native WebView2 gates before merge.

Fixes the product-level binder completeness gap without weakening FateDrop identity safeguards.

What changes:
- verified base printings can be persisted from exact two-source card agreement even when finish/edition identity remains quarantined;
- collector readiness, progress, dashboard summaries and set-completion use verified printings as the binder checklist authority;
- exact identities remain the authority for owned exact cards, pricing and valuation;
- printing-only missing cards expose no fake fateCardId and carry an explicit unresolved identity status.

Safety preserved:
- no fuzzy matching;
- first-edition composition remains quarantined;
- reverse-holo/finish rules unchanged;
- no unknown price becomes £0;
- no production activation or database write is performed by this PR.

Production audit motivating this:
- 157 verified sets;
- 136 binder-complete / 21 incomplete under identity-derived checklists;
- 213 missing underlying printings;
- 27,624 verified identities;
- 5,012 identities with usable market observations (~18.1%).

Key regression: a first-edition-held card can populate a verified binder printing slot while producing zero exact identities.

## Цель
Закрыть #67 и сделать локальную целостность документации обязательной частью CI.

## Реализация
- добавлен stdlib-only `tools/check_doc_links.py`;
- checker проверяет repository-relative Markdown links в root/docs/deploy, не делает network requests и блокирует path escape;
- добавлены unit tests для valid/missing/external/escape/fenced-code/image cases;
