## Linear

Fixes SHU-236.

## Problem

The private filesystem store could leave `.lock` behind when the lock handle's `close()` rejected, even after its snapshot committed. Nine enforced contract claims also lacked named regression controls and survived independent mutation testing.

## Change

- contains a rejected lock-handle close so it cannot skip the trailing lock unlink;
- adds the ten named SHU-236 controls for lock cleanup, immutable replacement scope/type, hardlinked state, root mode/ownership, configuration, hostile stored records and sizes, credential shape, clock rewind, and retired-record reachability;
- adds M1–M10, each required to fail its assigned named control without counting syntax/import/process crashes;
- wires both hardening commands into `npm test`;
- rejects configured non-default HTTPS ports because the required `NC-CONFIG` control exposed that merged main accepted them.

The original SHU-101 tests and mutations are byte-identical to main.

## Evidence

Exact head: `291ad755b74a183741684e40556f0ac4abf93235`  
Base: `b99da1ff00ffcc437142693f1cf9d0802cdc333f`  
Tree: `a2e51d89375a559781fb6873cc24ac1f40860682` — connector-published tree exactly matches the locally tested tree.

- test-first baseline: 8/10 controls passed; `NC-LOCK-RELEASE` reproduced EBADF and `NC-CONFIG` exposed non-default-port acceptance;
- new controls: 10/10 passed;
- new mutations: 10/10 killed by their named controls;
- original document controls: 19/19 passed unchanged;
- original mutations: 17/17 killed unchanged;
- platform: 239/239; actor assertion: 27/27; deployment: 9/9; web: 14/14;
- typecheck and diff check clean;
- coordinator: 579 passed, 5 known environment skips, 0 failed; zero coordinator/config files changed;
- hosted PostgreSQL and Git 2.43 jobs remain CI gates.

## Boundaries

R3, new-platform synthetic storage only. Four files changed. No authorization, delivery claims, retention queue contents, purge API, lock stealing, provider adapter, gateway mounting, legacy/production data, deployment, or activation. Dispatch remains disabled.

## Independent verification

Opus must verify this exact head after CI and review findings. Codex authored the head and cannot PASS it. Do not merge until Opus posts PASS at the same SHA.

